Privacy Policy for CatatIn

Effective Date: May 16, 2026

CatatIn is a note-taking application designed to help users create, organize, favorite, and archive personal notes. This Privacy Policy explains how CatatIn handles user information.

1. Information We Collect

CatatIn does not collect, store, or share any personal data from users.

The app allows users to create notes, categories, favorites, archives, and other note-related content. This information is stored locally on the user’s device and is not sent to any external server.

2. Local Data Storage

All notes and app data are stored locally on your device.

This may include:

Note titles
Note contents
Categories
Favorite notes
Archived notes
Note colors
Created and updated dates

CatatIn does not access this data remotely. The data remains on your device unless you delete the app or clear the app data.

3. Data Sharing

CatatIn does not share user data with third parties.

We do not sell, rent, trade, or transfer any user information to advertisers, analytics providers, or external services.

4. Internet Access

CatatIn does not require internet access for its main note-taking features.

If future versions include online features such as cloud backup or account login, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.

5. Permissions

CatatIn may only request permissions that are necessary for the app to function properly.

At this time, CatatIn does not require sensitive permissions such as location, camera, microphone, or contacts.

6. Children’s Privacy

CatatIn is not specifically directed toward children under the age of 13. The app does not knowingly collect personal information from children.

Since CatatIn does not collect personal data, no personal information from children is stored or shared.

7. Data Security

Because CatatIn stores notes locally on your device, users are responsible for maintaining the security of their own device.

We recommend using a screen lock, password, PIN, or biometric protection to keep your notes safe.

8. Data Deletion

Users can delete notes directly within the app.

Users may also remove all app data by uninstalling CatatIn or clearing the app data from the device settings.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with a new effective date.

Users are encouraged to review this Privacy Policy periodically.
